1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:07,000
Threatened by a ruthless demon, humanity was on the brink of destruction.

2
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:16,000
All seemed lost until a lone mage stepped forward and took up the fight.

3
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:29,000
After his triumph, he was hailed as the Wizard King, and his story became legend.

4
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:31,320
We came out on To火anza

5
00:00:32,760 --> 00:00:36,800
님

6
00:00:36,800 --> 00:00:42,680
This is what wasatrained by a отсuerdo that he Berechanalik

7
00:00:42,680 --> 00:00:44,060
We had no idea when we started.

8
00:00:44,060 --> 00:00:47,020
We were a drama team

9
00:00:47,020 --> 00:00:50,840
Actually, she was so inspiring man

10
00:00:50,840 --> 00:00:55,860
Why am I here, right?

11
00:00:55,860 --> 00:01:06,860
期待通りなどごめんなの自分でやれるからさ

12
00:01:06,860 --> 00:01:13,420
どうだっていい理屈ばっか張り付いた

13
00:01:13,420 --> 00:01:18,560
ハリボテの世界を生きてく

14
00:01:18,560 --> 00:01:28,560
誰かのためじゃない 今はまだ自分に追いつくまで

15
00:01:28,560 --> 00:01:36,560
かむしゃらでじめき飛ばした 体中の声が

16
00:01:36,560 --> 00:01:42,560
翼広げて どんな未来も舞うよ

17
00:01:42,560 --> 00:01:49,560
かぜうきて 自分を追い越すまで

18
00:02:12,560 --> 00:02:21,560
フォンゼル promotionか

19
00:02:21,560 --> 00:02:25,560
さおそろそろそろ

20
00:02:25,560 --> 00:02:28,560
どっても会いばかり

21
00:02:28,560 --> 00:02:30,560
彼に貴方を見た

22
00:02:30,560 --> 00:02:35,560
うちしいぶりだ

23
00:02:35,560 --> 00:02:39,560
彼は5ヶ月 sweetheart

24
00:02:39,560 --> 00:02:45,740
Asta and Yuno had received their grimoires, but they had not yet set out for the Magic

25
00:02:45,740 --> 00:02:49,740
Knight's entrance exam in the royal capital.

26
00:02:49,740 --> 00:02:54,060
Asta was camping in the woods near Hajj village, diligently training with the sword he had

27
00:02:54,060 --> 00:02:55,340
recently been given.

28
00:02:55,340 --> 00:03:12,580
I have no idea what I'm doing, at all, I mean I've never trained with a sword before in

29
00:03:12,580 --> 00:03:17,860
my life, I don't even know how I'm supposed to hold it, does hacking at trees really count

30
00:03:17,860 --> 00:03:18,860
as training?

31
00:03:18,860 --> 00:03:26,180
If I were you, kid, I would get out of the way and quickly, don't run right at me, hurry

32
00:03:26,180 --> 00:03:35,540
and jump to the side, take that!

33
00:03:35,540 --> 00:03:41,520
Very impressive, you took out that big guy in one blow, my mistake, I was doing some fishing

34
00:03:41,520 --> 00:03:47,860
in the river and I guess I must have wandered into the boar's territory, ha ha ha, yeah,

35
00:03:47,860 --> 00:03:51,180
anyway, name's Fonzal, I'm something of a nomad these days.

36
00:03:51,180 --> 00:03:53,180
Nice to meet you.

37
00:03:53,180 --> 00:03:54,180
Call me Zal.

38
00:03:54,180 --> 00:03:56,680
Okay, I'm Asta from Hajj village.

39
00:03:56,680 --> 00:04:00,360
It's a pleasure Asta, now tell me, are those yours?

40
00:04:00,360 --> 00:04:02,180
Yeah, why do you want to know?

41
00:04:02,180 --> 00:04:13,360
It's okay, I thought I was going to starve, I haven't eaten so much as a bite in two

42
00:04:13,360 --> 00:04:18,680
whole days, never did catch any fish.

43
00:04:18,680 --> 00:04:19,680
Awfully dense aren't they?

44
00:04:19,680 --> 00:04:23,680
It's amazing how they just suck all the moisture right out of your mouth.

45
00:04:23,680 --> 00:04:26,180
Yeah they do, so are you going to tell me why you're naked?

46
00:04:26,180 --> 00:04:30,280
I didn't want to get wet while I was fishing.

47
00:04:30,280 --> 00:04:31,680
What are these things?

48
00:04:31,680 --> 00:04:33,680
You just ate them without knowing?

49
00:04:33,680 --> 00:04:35,680
Some pot potatoes, a Hajj village specialty.

50
00:04:35,680 --> 00:04:36,680
Cool.

51
00:04:36,680 --> 00:04:37,680
Are you okay?

52
00:04:37,680 --> 00:04:38,680
Here you go.

53
00:04:38,680 --> 00:04:39,680
Yes, please.

54
00:04:39,680 --> 00:04:40,680
Thank you.

55
00:04:40,680 --> 00:04:41,680
What is this stuff?

56
00:04:41,680 --> 00:04:42,680
It's got such a bitter taste.

57
00:04:42,680 --> 00:04:43,680
It's my special Moguro leaf juice for increasing your magic power.

58
00:04:43,680 --> 00:04:44,680
Well, I'm certainly feeling better.

59
00:04:44,680 --> 00:04:49,680
If you don't mind coming to my house, maybe I can find a way to thank you for your help.

60
00:04:49,680 --> 00:04:50,680
Your house?

61
00:04:50,680 --> 00:05:05,680
Well, to be honest, I'm just kind of squatting there.

62
00:05:05,680 --> 00:05:09,680
I never knew there were places this nice way out in the woods.

63
00:05:09,680 --> 00:05:11,680
Every now and then you'll see one around.

64
00:05:11,680 --> 00:05:15,680
Guess I should go ahead and get some clothes on.

65
00:05:15,680 --> 00:05:21,680
Huh, a sword that can nullify magic.

66
00:05:21,680 --> 00:05:22,680
That's new to me.

67
00:05:22,680 --> 00:05:27,680
It's new to me too, but this baby is what's going to get me through the Magic Knights entrance exam.

68
00:05:27,680 --> 00:05:30,680
That's why I've been holed up here in the mountains training.

69
00:05:30,680 --> 00:05:31,680
Yeah, that's so?

70
00:05:31,680 --> 00:05:34,680
What brings an old guy like you up here anyway?

71
00:05:34,680 --> 00:05:35,680
Old guy, huh?

72
00:05:35,680 --> 00:05:38,680
I'm actually only 28, thank you very much.

73
00:05:38,680 --> 00:05:39,680
28?

74
00:05:39,680 --> 00:05:40,680
No way!

75
00:05:40,680 --> 00:05:43,680
Wow, you look so much older.

76
00:05:43,680 --> 00:05:46,680
Right, let's just leave that there.

77
00:05:50,680 --> 00:05:52,680
I'm waiting for someone.

78
00:05:52,680 --> 00:05:54,680
Kind of a weird meeting spot.

79
00:05:54,680 --> 00:05:56,680
It's complicated.

80
00:05:56,680 --> 00:05:57,680
Okay.

81
00:05:58,680 --> 00:06:01,680
So tell me, Asta, you're sleeping outside, right?

82
00:06:01,680 --> 00:06:04,680
Why not stay with me while you're training instead?

83
00:06:04,680 --> 00:06:06,680
Really? That'd be awesome, thanks!

84
00:06:06,680 --> 00:06:09,680
Hold on, are you just after my pot potatoes?

85
00:06:09,680 --> 00:06:12,680
Always treasure your encounters and connections with the people you meet.

86
00:06:12,680 --> 00:06:14,680
True, they may not have a concrete form.

87
00:06:14,680 --> 00:06:18,680
But those experiences will pile up in your heart and keep you company.

88
00:06:21,680 --> 00:06:23,680
Are you kidding me?

89
00:06:23,680 --> 00:06:25,680
This guy's obviously a total creep.

90
00:06:25,680 --> 00:06:27,680
Are you actually going to stay with him?

91
00:06:27,680 --> 00:06:29,680
Okay!

92
00:06:29,680 --> 00:06:31,680
I think I'll take you up on that!

93
00:06:31,680 --> 00:06:32,680
Thanks a lot, Mr. Zell!

94
00:06:32,680 --> 00:06:33,680
Great!

95
00:06:33,680 --> 00:06:35,680
Then let's talk about chores.

96
00:06:35,680 --> 00:06:36,680
How are you at Chopin' Wood?

97
00:06:36,680 --> 00:06:37,680
What?

98
00:06:37,680 --> 00:06:38,680
What?

99
00:06:50,680 --> 00:06:53,680
Man, this doesn't seem to be working at all.

100
00:06:54,680 --> 00:06:57,680
Well, maybe it's because all your weight is in your knees.

101
00:06:57,680 --> 00:06:58,680
Huh?

102
00:06:58,680 --> 00:07:03,680
The problem you've been having is that you can't manage a second blow once you swing your sword, right?

103
00:07:03,680 --> 00:07:05,680
It throws off your balance.

104
00:07:05,680 --> 00:07:06,680
Uh, yeah.

105
00:07:06,680 --> 00:07:08,680
I know something that might help with that.

106
00:07:08,680 --> 00:07:11,680
Keep your toes pointed in the same direction as your sword.

107
00:07:11,680 --> 00:07:14,680
Then you take a half step forward with your right foot to shift your weight.

108
00:07:14,680 --> 00:07:15,680
Go on, try.

109
00:07:15,680 --> 00:07:16,680
Woohoo!

110
00:07:16,680 --> 00:07:33,680
I did it, I can't believe I actually made it up to the second swing!

111
00:07:33,680 --> 00:07:34,680
Ah yeah, you did it.

112
00:07:34,680 --> 00:07:35,680
Pick it up pretty fast, too.

113
00:07:35,680 --> 00:07:36,680
That was impressive.

114
00:07:36,680 --> 00:07:37,680
No more pulling over!

115
00:07:37,680 --> 00:07:38,680
That was amazing!

116
00:07:38,680 --> 00:07:40,680
How'd you know that trick?

117
00:07:40,680 --> 00:07:41,680
You fight with swords, too?

118
00:07:41,680 --> 00:07:44,680
Well, no, not swords, exactly.

119
00:07:44,680 --> 00:07:45,880
Hold on a sec.

120
00:07:53,460 --> 00:07:55,220
Wind creation magic.

121
00:07:55,620 --> 00:07:57,020
Emperor of slashing winds.

122
00:08:04,040 --> 00:08:04,560
Whoa!

123
00:08:05,160 --> 00:08:05,960
So cool!

124
00:08:09,400 --> 00:08:11,100
You see, it's not a true sword,

125
00:08:11,200 --> 00:08:13,380
but rather my magic taking on the shape of one.

126
00:08:13,380 --> 00:08:15,380
It's the emperor of slashing winds.

127
00:08:15,380 --> 00:08:17,080
I call it Slashy for short.

128
00:08:17,080 --> 00:08:19,380
You're awesome at naming stuff, too?

129
00:08:19,380 --> 00:08:21,380
Well, anyway, working with this thing

130
00:08:21,380 --> 00:08:23,380
is how I picked up a little swordsmanship.

131
00:08:23,380 --> 00:08:24,800
Hey, then can you teach me?

132
00:08:24,800 --> 00:08:26,560
I'm sure anything you know will help.

133
00:08:26,560 --> 00:08:27,560
I don't know.

134
00:08:27,560 --> 00:08:29,400
Just a few lessons, that's all!

135
00:08:29,400 --> 00:08:31,400
Please, I'll work hard!

136
00:08:31,400 --> 00:08:32,900
Sure, no problem.

137
00:08:34,400 --> 00:08:35,400
Sounds good.

138
00:08:35,400 --> 00:08:37,400
It does, really?

139
00:08:38,400 --> 00:08:40,400
Awesome, thank you so much!

140
00:08:40,400 --> 00:08:41,400
Alright, yes!

141
00:08:41,400 --> 00:08:43,140
I've got a teacher!

142
00:08:43,140 --> 00:08:44,480
Oh, yeah!

143
00:08:44,480 --> 00:08:46,040
Awesome! Awesome!

144
00:08:46,040 --> 00:08:47,140
So cool!

145
00:08:47,140 --> 00:08:49,140
Yes! Yes! Yes! Yes!

146
00:08:49,140 --> 00:08:52,140
However, there's one thing I want you to promise me in return.

147
00:08:53,220 --> 00:08:56,220
Asta, why are you working so hard to get stronger?

148
00:08:56,220 --> 00:08:58,260
To become the Wizard King!

149
00:08:58,260 --> 00:08:59,260
Ah.

150
00:09:00,160 --> 00:09:02,020
I see. Well, that's good.

151
00:09:02,020 --> 00:09:03,760
Yes, it's very good.

152
00:09:03,760 --> 00:09:05,400
Wait, you're not gonna laugh?

153
00:09:05,400 --> 00:09:06,900
No, why would I do that?

154
00:09:06,900 --> 00:09:08,900
Because it's impossible or whatever?

155
00:09:08,900 --> 00:09:12,900
But how can you know whether or not something is impossible until you give it a try?

156
00:09:13,900 --> 00:09:14,900
Listen closely.

157
00:09:15,900 --> 00:09:17,900
I want you to make me a promise, Asta,

158
00:09:17,900 --> 00:09:20,980
that you'll only ever use what I teach you to make that dream come true.

159
00:09:20,980 --> 00:09:22,920
Sure. What's that mean, though?

160
00:09:22,920 --> 00:09:29,920
Just don't use what you learn here for evil. Use it to achieve your goals. Not as a tool for harming the innocent or bullying people.

161
00:09:29,920 --> 00:09:32,920
I don't need anybody to tell me not to do that stuff.

162
00:09:32,920 --> 00:09:34,260
So you promise?

163
00:09:34,260 --> 00:09:36,260
Yeah, I promise.

164
00:09:36,260 --> 00:09:39,260
Okay, then let's get to work.

165
00:09:39,260 --> 00:09:41,260
Right! I'm ready whenever you are!

166
00:09:41,260 --> 00:09:44,260
No! You're too slow!

167
00:09:44,260 --> 00:09:51,260
Don't pause between hits. What we're after is rapid-fire attack.

168
00:09:51,260 --> 00:09:52,260
Right!

169
00:09:52,260 --> 00:09:59,260
You really are fantastic, Asta. Your defense and offense are both solid, and your footwork is improving, too.

170
00:09:59,260 --> 00:10:03,260
What I don't understand is if you're this strong, then why didn't you just take care of that giant boar yourself?

171
00:10:03,260 --> 00:10:12,260
Without either a sword or my grimoire on me, there wasn't a lot I could do. And besides, my skills with the sword aren't anything particularly advanced. You just seem to be especially good at putting them to use.

172
00:10:12,260 --> 00:10:30,260
I don't know. I think it's because you're especially good at teaching them.

173
00:10:30,260 --> 00:10:33,260
I think it's because you're especially good at teaching them.

174
00:10:33,260 --> 00:10:37,260
I did do some teachery stuff once upon a time, so maybe.

175
00:10:37,260 --> 00:10:39,260
Oh, really?

176
00:10:39,260 --> 00:10:41,940
The students that I taught didn't think very much of me, though.

177
00:10:43,060 --> 00:10:45,240
You know, I've had more than a hundred pupils.

178
00:10:45,920 --> 00:10:49,400
But the way you're progressing, you might rank among the top three at least.

179
00:10:50,000 --> 00:10:50,900
The top three?

180
00:10:51,640 --> 00:10:52,780
Top two, maybe.

181
00:10:53,300 --> 00:10:58,500
The highest ranked is kind of out there, not even using the sword as a sword, so I don't know if that really counts.

182
00:10:59,720 --> 00:11:06,740
Well, anyway, even if you are accepted into a Magic Knight squad, I think you'll turn out to be a respectably skilled swordsman.

183
00:11:07,520 --> 00:11:08,960
You really think so?

184
00:11:09,260 --> 00:11:12,460
Then let's go! We've got some more training to do!

185
00:11:12,880 --> 00:11:15,860
Whoa, not so fast. We aren't even done eating yet.

186
00:11:18,140 --> 00:11:22,000
Several more days passed, until a visitor arrived.

187
00:11:24,620 --> 00:11:27,540
I've returned, Master. Sorry it took so long.

188
00:11:28,220 --> 00:11:28,740
Who's that?

189
00:11:29,160 --> 00:11:31,760
You're back. So, what did you find out, Mariella?

190
00:11:32,340 --> 00:11:32,940
Mariella?

191
00:11:34,160 --> 00:11:38,920
One of my pupils. She's helping me. I've asked her to track down my fiancée.

192
00:11:38,920 --> 00:11:41,560
That girl's your student?

193
00:11:42,120 --> 00:11:46,060
If you need to find your fiancée, wouldn't it be better just to go out and look for her yourself?

194
00:11:46,960 --> 00:11:51,880
The full explanation is a bit complicated, but I can't draw attention to myself right now.

195
00:11:51,880 --> 00:12:00,920
I'm Asta from Hajj Village. The old man here is teaching me how to use the sword. Nice to meet you.

196
00:12:02,540 --> 00:12:08,060
Please, this is no ordinary old man. While it might be true that he's old, he is an amazing old man.

197
00:12:08,060 --> 00:12:14,760
So, look, I don't know who you are, but you should keep in mind that he is not the kind of old man that you can casually refer to as old man.

198
00:12:14,880 --> 00:12:16,620
There are rules to follow for this sort of thing.

199
00:12:16,880 --> 00:12:22,780
Like I told you, I'm Asta from Hajj Village, and I don't see what's so wrong about calling an old man, old man!

200
00:12:22,920 --> 00:12:24,580
It's a simple matter of perception.

201
00:12:24,940 --> 00:12:29,840
If you truly realized how amazing he was, you would be addressing him with the proper amount of respect and deference.

202
00:12:30,200 --> 00:12:33,820
But when you say old man, it doesn't sound the least bit respectful or deferential.

203
00:12:33,820 --> 00:12:36,680
How am I supposed to make the words old man sound respectful?

204
00:12:36,680 --> 00:12:38,840
Maybe we could just let it go now, huh?

205
00:12:38,960 --> 00:12:42,840
Listening to you two bicker isn't exactly doing wonders for my self-esteem.

206
00:12:44,380 --> 00:12:48,180
So what about Dominante? Where is she?

207
00:12:48,860 --> 00:12:55,840
Forgive me, Master. I don't know how to say this, but I believe it's possible that Domina has passed away.

208
00:12:58,080 --> 00:12:59,000
Oh, no.

209
00:13:00,000 --> 00:13:03,420
And so, Fonzel shared his story with Asta.

210
00:13:04,560 --> 00:13:08,640
Fonzel and his fiancée, Dominante, had been members of the Diamond Kingdom's army.

211
00:13:10,020 --> 00:13:18,220
No longer able to stomach the army's extreme methods, the couple plotted to desert but wound up separated as they sought to escape the kingdom's assassin.

212
00:13:18,880 --> 00:13:25,660
Desperate to find his fiancée, Fonzel asked his former pupil and fellow deserter, Mariela, to search for her while he laid low.

213
00:13:25,660 --> 00:13:29,980
Fonzel knew that when he made a move, the killer would, too.

214
00:13:30,480 --> 00:13:36,900
Not wanting to endanger Domina if she were in hiding nearby, he was forced to go to ground in an abandoned house.

215
00:13:36,900 --> 00:13:38,900
Wow.

216
00:13:40,340 --> 00:13:41,640
Here's Domina's wand.

217
00:13:42,640 --> 00:13:45,340
He was found where the assassin was thought to have attacked her.

218
00:13:46,280 --> 00:13:49,160
That, and a great deal of blood.

219
00:13:49,980 --> 00:13:50,540
I see.

220
00:13:50,540 --> 00:13:54,200
If you'll excuse me, I need a moment to myself now.

221
00:13:54,200 --> 00:14:16,640
Master, pardon me.

222
00:14:16,640 --> 00:14:23,980
I'm sorry, but there's something I need to talk to you about.

223
00:14:24,600 --> 00:14:28,520
Back when you helped me in the other students' escape, do you remember?

224
00:14:30,020 --> 00:14:30,580
Yeah.

225
00:14:32,480 --> 00:14:34,300
How's everyone doing these days?

226
00:14:34,860 --> 00:14:35,460
Oh, wow.

227
00:14:36,060 --> 00:14:38,000
That actually got a smile out of you.

228
00:14:38,580 --> 00:14:42,660
You know, it's funny that you ask because everyone else but me is dead.

229
00:14:42,660 --> 00:14:43,520
Huh?

230
00:14:46,760 --> 00:14:49,640
They were murdered by the Diamond Kingdom's assassin.

231
00:14:51,580 --> 00:14:53,160
Every last one of them.

232
00:14:58,960 --> 00:15:00,560
What the hell are you doing?

233
00:15:01,340 --> 00:15:02,760
This is my job now.

234
00:15:02,920 --> 00:15:07,960
I do the kingdom's dirty work, provide it with useful intel, and dispose of its defectors when necessary.

235
00:15:07,960 --> 00:15:12,820
If I hadn't agreed to cooperate with them, then I would be as dead as the others are now.

236
00:15:13,860 --> 00:15:14,860
Don't worry, though.

237
00:15:14,900 --> 00:15:16,380
We aren't going to kill you here.

238
00:15:16,680 --> 00:15:19,760
I was given specific instructions to bring you back alive.

239
00:15:20,140 --> 00:15:23,920
And in case you're thinking of trying to escape, you should know this building is surrounded.

240
00:15:25,840 --> 00:15:28,600
That mage knight has entered the final stages.

241
00:15:29,060 --> 00:15:32,760
We'll need your advice on finishing touches to ensure proper functionality.

242
00:15:34,040 --> 00:15:36,600
That is where you were previously stationed, I believe.

243
00:15:36,600 --> 00:15:38,820
It's Mars.

244
00:15:38,960 --> 00:15:39,360
Sorry.

245
00:15:40,360 --> 00:15:42,460
The boy has a name and it's Mars.

246
00:15:42,880 --> 00:15:45,240
Stop talking about him like he's some kind of weapon.

247
00:15:45,800 --> 00:15:46,380
All right.

248
00:15:46,920 --> 00:15:48,760
Doesn't matter to me one way or another.

249
00:15:51,560 --> 00:15:52,780
Are you okay?

250
00:15:54,080 --> 00:15:54,740
And you!

251
00:15:54,860 --> 00:15:55,740
What's your problem?

252
00:15:55,840 --> 00:15:58,200
Aren't you grateful for what the old man's done for you?

253
00:15:58,980 --> 00:15:59,940
Yes, I am.

254
00:15:59,940 --> 00:16:05,080
I recognize that the combat techniques he taught me when I was his student are what's helped to keep me alive,

255
00:16:05,180 --> 00:16:06,760
and for that he still has my respect.

256
00:16:07,060 --> 00:16:10,600
If he didn't, why would I ever be concerned with the way in which you address him?

257
00:16:10,840 --> 00:16:13,100
But then why would you do something like this?

258
00:16:13,360 --> 00:16:16,700
If I fixated on those details, I could never get my job done.

259
00:16:18,380 --> 00:16:20,300
So would you kindly not interfere?

260
00:16:20,840 --> 00:16:23,360
I doubt you want to die for an old man you don't know.

261
00:16:24,220 --> 00:16:26,740
I'd say that I know him pretty well by now!

262
00:16:27,060 --> 00:16:27,820
No, Asta.

263
00:16:28,360 --> 00:16:30,080
Please just listen to Mariela.

264
00:16:30,420 --> 00:16:31,520
You have to get out of here.

265
00:16:31,720 --> 00:16:32,680
You promised me.

266
00:16:33,580 --> 00:16:37,440
You said you'd only ever use what I taught you about the sword to achieve your dream.

267
00:16:37,820 --> 00:16:42,120
You shouldn't use your skills here in defense of some random old man, so get going.

268
00:16:42,540 --> 00:16:43,180
I mean it.

269
00:16:43,280 --> 00:16:43,560
Run!

270
00:16:43,560 --> 00:16:46,600
Like I said, you're not just some random old man to me!

271
00:16:46,920 --> 00:16:48,460
Hey, don't worry about it.

272
00:16:48,840 --> 00:16:52,060
I may be old, but I can still handle these goons without your help.

273
00:16:52,060 --> 00:16:54,060
You're already wounded!

274
00:16:55,700 --> 00:16:57,280
I'll make my own promise.

275
00:16:57,400 --> 00:17:00,220
I swear not to die at the hands of these diamond mages.

276
00:17:00,800 --> 00:17:02,320
I'm gonna hold you to it!

277
00:17:02,820 --> 00:17:04,500
No dying until I see you again!

278
00:17:04,560 --> 00:17:05,480
You understand me?

279
00:17:05,820 --> 00:17:06,240
Right.

280
00:17:08,800 --> 00:17:09,960
I'm sorry, Asta.

281
00:17:10,960 --> 00:17:12,200
This is for the best.

282
00:17:14,340 --> 00:17:14,700
Domina.

283
00:17:14,700 --> 00:17:34,340
Asta.

284
00:17:34,340 --> 00:17:35,700
Please.

285
00:17:36,100 --> 00:17:37,340
I don't care what happens.

286
00:17:38,640 --> 00:17:40,280
There's no hope left in me.

287
00:17:41,520 --> 00:17:42,900
No reason to go on.

288
00:17:43,700 --> 00:17:45,920
I'm so very tired of all of this.

289
00:17:46,520 --> 00:17:47,700
Just get out of here.

290
00:17:48,220 --> 00:17:48,920
Leave me be.

291
00:17:48,920 --> 00:17:50,920
No way!

292
00:17:52,920 --> 00:17:58,240
A reason to live?

293
00:17:58,620 --> 00:17:59,500
To keep going?

294
00:17:59,780 --> 00:18:00,380
To hope?

295
00:18:00,880 --> 00:18:02,460
Life doesn't just hand you those.

296
00:18:03,140 --> 00:18:04,160
It takes work.

297
00:18:04,560 --> 00:18:06,260
You have to fight to find them yourself.

298
00:18:06,260 --> 00:18:11,340
If you're done moping, I could use a little help here.

299
00:18:11,340 --> 00:18:27,620
Wind creation magic.

300
00:18:28,080 --> 00:18:29,620
Emperor of slashing winds.

301
00:18:30,620 --> 00:18:31,500
Winter wind.

302
00:18:37,340 --> 00:18:40,800
That spell allows me to send out a lot of slashies at once.

303
00:18:40,800 --> 00:18:42,640
I call it the Flying One.

304
00:18:43,040 --> 00:18:43,440
Wow!

305
00:18:43,520 --> 00:18:44,620
What an awesome name!

306
00:18:44,940 --> 00:18:46,760
You saw me at a very ugly moment.

307
00:18:47,320 --> 00:18:48,460
I'm feeling better now.

308
00:18:48,540 --> 00:18:49,100
Don't worry.

309
00:18:49,340 --> 00:18:49,680
Good.

310
00:18:50,420 --> 00:18:51,060
Behind you.

311
00:18:54,100 --> 00:18:57,840
He negated my spell?

312
00:19:00,900 --> 00:19:02,160
What's wrong, old man?

313
00:19:02,600 --> 00:19:04,320
Have you decided to give up after all?

314
00:19:04,660 --> 00:19:08,340
We each get to choose for ourselves when the time has come to admit defeat.

315
00:19:08,340 --> 00:19:11,760
And thanks to you, I realized that for me, that day isn't today.

316
00:19:12,260 --> 00:19:15,600
There's no way I'm about to let this bunch of idiots end me now.

317
00:19:16,400 --> 00:19:17,220
We're withdrawing.

318
00:19:17,940 --> 00:19:18,140
Huh?

319
00:19:18,560 --> 00:19:19,540
I'll bring up the rear.

320
00:19:20,060 --> 00:19:21,040
Round up any casualties.

321
00:19:21,620 --> 00:19:22,880
I want an orderly retreat.

322
00:19:22,880 --> 00:19:25,440
You guys are just leaving?

323
00:19:25,440 --> 00:19:30,900
When you're staging an attack, make sure to go in with at least three times the number of troops as your target.

324
00:19:31,700 --> 00:19:33,660
If your number is halved, change tactics.

325
00:19:34,160 --> 00:19:35,360
If halved again, retreat.

326
00:19:36,080 --> 00:19:39,120
Or, so a certain instructor of mine told me once.

327
00:19:39,920 --> 00:19:42,040
Don't think for a second that this is over, though.

328
00:19:42,640 --> 00:19:45,240
I'll spend my whole life on your trail if I have to.

329
00:19:45,580 --> 00:19:46,720
That's fine by me.

330
00:19:47,000 --> 00:19:49,120
As of today, I've decided I'm done running.

331
00:19:49,660 --> 00:19:51,680
From you, from myself, from anybody.

332
00:19:52,400 --> 00:19:53,980
And I'm done being a coward.

333
00:19:54,680 --> 00:19:56,640
Domina is out there somewhere alive.

334
00:19:56,980 --> 00:19:58,020
I know she is.

335
00:19:58,440 --> 00:20:00,540
I'll find her, no matter what.

336
00:20:00,840 --> 00:20:02,360
So you just try to keep up.

337
00:20:03,180 --> 00:20:04,340
You hear that, Mariela?

338
00:20:04,560 --> 00:20:07,740
I hope you're ready to deal with his old man smell for the rest of your life!

339
00:20:08,200 --> 00:20:09,780
Will you stop talking, please?

340
00:20:09,780 --> 00:20:10,840
Words can wound.

341
00:20:11,540 --> 00:20:13,640
I guess we'll both do our best, huh?

342
00:20:15,240 --> 00:20:19,440
And, I think you might be learning the proper way to say old man.

343
00:20:20,080 --> 00:20:20,880
Keep practicing.

344
00:20:27,700 --> 00:20:29,360
Are you really leaving already?

345
00:20:29,860 --> 00:20:33,080
Yeah, I'll keep looking for Domina no matter how long it takes.

346
00:20:33,280 --> 00:20:37,700
When I finally have her, I'll try to find a way to atone for all the harm I've done in my life.

347
00:20:38,060 --> 00:20:43,760
I haven't figured out exactly how I'll manage that yet, but considering my past, it'll probably take many years.

348
00:20:43,760 --> 00:20:46,880
Which means, I won't be dying anytime soon.

349
00:20:47,460 --> 00:20:49,880
You're the one I have to thank for giving me that resolve.

350
00:20:50,600 --> 00:20:51,920
I'm just glad I could help.

351
00:20:51,920 --> 00:20:57,320
I should get going, or it's going to get too hard to say goodbye.

352
00:20:57,820 --> 00:20:58,160
See ya.

353
00:20:58,160 --> 00:20:58,260
Right.

354
00:20:59,620 --> 00:21:00,320
Hey, wait!

355
00:21:00,700 --> 00:21:02,740
You're seriously going to leave just like that?

356
00:21:03,180 --> 00:21:03,980
Sure am.

357
00:21:04,300 --> 00:21:06,600
See, I'm a guy who likes to get things done.

358
00:21:06,980 --> 00:21:10,140
I've been sitting around for too long, and now I'm ready to get to work.

359
00:21:10,480 --> 00:21:11,800
Just like you should be doing.

360
00:21:12,560 --> 00:21:13,380
Time's a-wasting.

361
00:21:14,120 --> 00:21:15,240
What does that mean?

362
00:21:15,240 --> 00:21:20,580
You're a guy who likes to get things done too, aren't you?

363
00:21:21,080 --> 00:21:21,940
So get going.

364
00:21:22,520 --> 00:21:23,680
There's no reason to wait.

365
00:21:23,780 --> 00:21:26,400
You have everything you need to start making your dream come true.

366
00:21:27,860 --> 00:21:31,220
Come on, now's when you decide to get all teacher-y on me, old man?

367
00:21:31,900 --> 00:21:32,540
See ya!

368
00:21:32,940 --> 00:21:33,660
Good luck!

369
00:21:34,180 --> 00:21:35,700
Go become the Wizard King!

370
00:21:36,700 --> 00:21:37,460
All right.

371
00:21:38,120 --> 00:21:39,540
Guess I'll head back to the village.

372
00:21:39,540 --> 00:21:48,600
Actually, I've got one last lesson for you.

373
00:21:48,680 --> 00:21:50,420
Take this monster down, will you?

374
00:21:50,560 --> 00:21:51,060
No way!

375
00:21:51,120 --> 00:21:52,280
You can do it yourself!

376
00:21:52,440 --> 00:21:53,980
And why are you naked this time?

377
00:21:54,060 --> 00:21:55,700
Don't tell me you were fishing again!

378
00:21:56,000 --> 00:21:57,320
I'll explain later!

379
00:21:57,640 --> 00:21:58,320
Just help!

380
00:21:58,320 --> 00:21:58,980
